CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*cmd->t_bidi_data_sg)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct scatterlist)...)
#79: FILE: drivers/target/target_core_transport.c:2110:
+	cmd->t_bidi_data_sg = kmalloc(sizeof(struct scatterlist) * nents, GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

